 cost of capital of 9.7%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.53).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.66x.","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 34%.","ROE of 12% is amplified by 7.0x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","Operating margin is running 34pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.7% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.8x net debt to EBITDA ($8.7M of cash against $468.4M of debt), above the 1.5x gate, and interest cover is thin at 2.8x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 0.57 in the distress zone."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.6% over 3 years, 5.2% over 5 years and 3.3% over 10 years.","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 4.9% a year over five years.","Capex runs 2.4x depreciation (47.5% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders own 46.6%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 47%.","Insiders have only bought over the past year (3 purchases, net $104K bought).","It returns 5.5% a year to shareholders (8.3% in dividends, less 0.3% of net share issuance).","The share count has grown 0.8% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It pays out 251% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["With about 156 employees, each generates about $1.9M of revenue, 0.8x the Real Estate median, and revenue has grown 3.7% a year across its filed history.","CEO pay is $159K (0x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $13K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":43,"head":"Avoid: priced 209% above its fair value of $9.17.","pros":["Composite 42, above the 39 line (gates 11/25)","2 analysts' mean target $42.00 (+48%)","Insiders net buyers ($104K over 12 months)","Returns 5.5% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 209% above fair value of $9.1